# 1. Starting point: do not assume a vector space

The previous static formulation

$$
K_t\subseteq\mathcal K
$$

is insufficient as a **candidate representation** if research demonstrates that the set of represented distinctions itself can change.

However, this does **not** yet establish that KnowledgeOS is a vector space.

Therefore we introduce only:

$$
\boxed{\mathcal D_t}
$$

as a candidate set of currently represented distinction-bearing dimensions.

We also allow:

$$
\boxed{
\mathcal D_t\neq\mathcal D_{t+1}.
}
$$

This is the primary hypothesis.

It means that state evolution may change not only the values represented, but also **which distinctions are represented**.

The uploaded formulation correctly identifies this as the important difference between value evolution and structural evolution. 

