# 2. Candidate universal dimension domain

We may hypothesize the existence of a larger set

$$
\mathcal D_\infty
$$

such that

$$
\mathcal D_t\subseteq\mathcal D_\infty.
$$

But:

$$
\boxed{
|\mathcal D_\infty|=\infty
}
$$

must remain an **open hypothesis**.

We must not yet write:

$$
\dim(\mathcal K_\infty)=\aleph_0
$$

because the word **dimension** there presupposes a vector-space or analogous algebraic structure.

The uploaded document currently makes exactly that stronger assumption. 

The safe formulation is:

> There may exist an unbounded or potentially infinite universe of candidate distinctions.

That is sufficient for current research.

