# 3. Dimension must be derived from D4.5

The previous definition

$$
D_i=\text{an independently discriminable aspect}
$$

should be weakened.

### Candidate Definition D5.2.1 — Distinction-Bearing Dimension

A candidate dimension \(D_i\) is a representation-level object associated with a distinction that can be detected by one or more admissible observations under a specified inquiry and context.

Thus:

$$
D_i
\leadsto
\{o_\alpha\}_{\alpha\in A_i}.
$$

A dimension is not primitive merely because somebody names it.

It must eventually pass the D5 tests:

$$
\boxed{
Necessary
\land
Irreducible
\land
NonReconstructible.
}
$$

This connects directly to today's D4.5/D5 minimality work.

