and seek a representation

$$
\rho:
\mathcal S_{\rm req}
\rightarrow
R(\mathcal D_t,V_t,\ldots)
$$

such that:

### Faithfulness

$$
\ker(\rho)\subseteq\sim_{\rm req}.
$$

### Exact realization

$$
\ker(\rho)=\sim_{\rm req}.
$$

### Irreducibility

Removing a candidate component violates faithfulness.

### Non-reconstructibility

The removed component cannot be derived from the remaining representation.

### Congruence

Mandatory operations remain well-defined after quotienting.

Only if all five survive do we have a candidate minimal carrier.

